  "worked_solution": "A function $f(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={f}^{\u2033}(x)$, we can see that ${f}^{\u2033}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-5,-1)$ and  $(1,5).$  Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is concave up on the intervals $(-5,-1)$ and  $(1,5).$",
